Subject: [PATCH 11334/11362] Correction: the zero-engine tool-grammar trial
 was the 0.8B, not the 27B

The operator challenged the result, noting the 27B has produced world models
during induction. The challenge was right and exposed a relay error of mine: I
reported "the real 27B produced zero engines" when the branch's own summary line
reads "Real 0.8B loop". The trial used the 0.5 GB CPU smoke model, and the task
scoped itself honestly in two places -- one of which I had quoted correctly in an
earlier report before contradicting it in a later one.

The mechanism is the reusable part. The status entry said "the real model", and I
mapped that onto the pinned model because the surrounding text was about it. The
branch names the model one screen away. Reading a label instead of opening the
value, committed in a relay rather than in code, where it is hardest to catch.

The substance also favours the operator's instinct. The same branch records 29 of
37 scored world-model inductions on a 27B, and 31 tokens in 11.29 s with a
parseable call whose code argument is missing is the signature of a grammar that
admits an envelope without requiring the payload -- a schema defect, not evidence
about a model.

Corrected status: the arm is UNTESTED on the pinned model, not tested-and-failed.
A bounded 27B trial is dispatched on GPU 1 at n_ctx 49152, with the grammar to be
tested first without a model, since a grammar is deterministic and an admitted
code-less candidate would make every model result uninterpretable.

