+## 2026-09-05 22:35Z — CORRECTION: the zero-engine trial was the 0.8B, not the 27B; 27B trial authorised
+
+The operator asked whether some other failure was getting in the way of the tool-grammar result,
+noting that the 27B has produced world models during induction. That challenge was correct and it
+exposed a relay error of mine.
+
+**What I told the operator:** "the real 27B produced ZERO engines."
+**What the branch says**, in its own summary line on `outer-loop/kv-persistence-confirm`:
+`Real 0.8B loop: two parseable calls, missing required code, zero engines.`
+
+The trial ran on Qwen3.5-0.8B, the 0.5 GB CPU smoke model. The task scoped itself honestly in two
+places — "This says nothing about the pinned 27B's tool syntax" and "27B trials remain deferred" —
+and I quoted the first of those correctly in an earlier report before contradicting it in a later
+one.
+
+**How the error happened, since it is the reusable part.** The status entry says "the real model
+produced zero engines". I mapped "the real model" onto the pinned 27B because the surrounding
+paragraphs are about the 27B. The branch names the model one screen away. I read a LABEL instead of
+opening the value — the defect this project has recorded repeatedly, committed in a relay rather
+than in code, which is where it is hardest to see.
+
+**Why the operator's instinct was right on the substance too.** The same branch records
+"world-model inductions tonight (ThinkingCap-27B + Qwen-9B, generous token budgets), 29/37 scored".
+The pinned model demonstrably produces engines on the ordinary induce path. And 31 tokens in
+11.29 s with a PARSEABLE call whose code argument is MISSING is the signature of a grammar that
+admits an envelope without requiring the payload — a schema defect, not evidence about a model.
+
+**Corrected status of the arm: UNTESTED on the pinned model, not tested-and-failed.** Those are
+different conclusions and the second would have retired a direction nobody has tried.
+
+**Authorised and dispatched:** a bounded 27B trial on GPU 1, ~45 minutes, `CARNOT_ARC_INDUCE_N_CTX=49152`
+because 98304 spans both cards and a two-card commitment is not authorised. The brief requires the
+GRAMMAR to be tested first, without a model — a grammar is deterministic, and if it accepts a
+code-less candidate then no model result is interpretable until that is fixed. Arm and control on
+the same model, same prompts, same seed; n stated; a control that also produces nothing means the
+harness is broken rather than the arm.
+
